<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Walter Devereux, 1st Earl of Essex</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1541">1541</a>–<a href="/years/1576">1576</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Walter Devereux, 1st Earl of Essex, was an English nobleman who in 1573 led a private venture, backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a>, to colonise Clandeboye in Ulster. The enterprise was marked by brutality, including the seizure and execution of Sir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brian-macphelim-oneill">Brian MacPhelim O'Neill</a> in 1574 and the massacre on Rathlin Island in 1575, and it failed. He died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a> as Earl Marshal of Ireland and was the father of Elizabeth's favourite, Robert Devereux.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/walter-devereux-1st-earl-of-essex.jpg" alt="Walter Devereux, 1st Earl of Essex" width="320" height="445" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Walter_Devereux,_1st_Earl_of_Essex_from_NPG.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
